        "# Coroutine function\n",
        "\n",
        "A coroutine function is normally defined with `async def` and, unlike an asynchronous generator function, does not contain `yield`. Calling it creates a coroutine object.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-coroutine-function)"
      ]
    }
